      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 2 at 3:33AM HST until November 2 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI AND OAHU...\n...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH FACING SHORES OF MOLOKAI AND\nMAUI...\n\n.A moderate, long-period north-northwest (340 degrees) swell will\ngradually decline today, with surf falling below advisory levels\nby this evening.\n\n* WHAT...Surf along north facing shores of 14 to 18 feet this\nmorning, subsiding to 10 to 14 feet tonight. For west facing\nshores, surf 10 to 15 feet this morning, subsiding to 7 to 10\nfeet by tonight.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai and\nOahu, and north facing shores of Molokai and Maui.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
      "instruction": "Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't\ngo out.",
